# --- environment -------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# --- large or non-redistributable inputs --------------------------------------
# Raw incident downloads hold point-level coordinates. The paper's ethics
# statement commits to distributing retrieval scripts and the aggregated
# analytic units rather than republishing raw point records, and some municipal
# portals restrict redistribution. Everything here is re-derivable from
# data/interim/registry.csv and registry_arcgis.csv.
#
# Matched at any depth, not just the repository root: `data/raw/` on its own is
# anchored by its slash, so a stray src/data/raw/ or an unpacked archive holding
# nested/data/raw/ would not have been caught. This is the one exclusion that
# carries an ethics commitment, so it should not depend on where the directory
# happens to land.
**/data/raw/
**/cache/

# Superseded intermediate panels. cells/ predates the building-footprint
# exposure rebuild; cells_exposure/ is the version every reported result uses
# and IS tracked.
data/interim/cells/
data/interim/cells_preclassifierfix/
data/interim/sf_cells.parquet
data/interim/probe_raw.csv

# --- build products ------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.aux
*.out
*.synctex.gz
**/outputs/logs/

# --- not part of this study ----------------------------------------------------
# Unrelated coursework that happens to share this directory. It all lives under
# archive/, which is excluded wholesale further down, so the per-file rules that
# used to sit here were vestigial -- and one of them spelled out the author's
# name in a tracked file, which is the sort of thing this repository is
# otherwise careful about. The directory rule is the one doing the work.
archive/

# Working documents kept local: an internal reference explicitly marked not for
# circulation, and a commissioned external review of the manuscript.
Crime_and_Slope_Project_Guide.pdf
GUIDE.md
deep-research-report.md

# --- manuscript and submission material ----------------------------------------
# This repository is the replication package: code, the aggregated panels it runs
# on, and the tables it produces. The paper, its supplement, the analysis plan,
# the journal checklist and the conference deck live with the submission, not
# here.
#
# The directory rules below are what actually does the work now, since every
# manuscript file lives under paper/ and every assembled bundle under packages/.
# Directory patterns with a trailing slash and no leading slash match at any
# depth, so these hold wherever the directory is created.
paper/
packages/
submission/
jqc_submission/
archive/

# Individual filenames, kept as a second line of defence in case a document is
# ever written outside those directories. This list is a denylist of exact
# names, which is precisely how jqc_manuscript.tex got tracked once: the rule
# named the PLOS manuscript and not the JQC one, so the anonymised manuscript,
# the title page carrying the author's name and ORCID, and both full packages
# sat in a public repository. Anything added here is a name that has already
# escaped; prefer putting new documents under paper/.
plos_manuscript.tex
manuscript_general.tex
jqc_manuscript.tex
jqc_title_page.tex
Cover_Letter.pdf
PREREGISTRATION.md
SUPPLEMENT.md
SUBMISSION.md
PAPER.md
RESEARCH.md
DIRECTION.md
PILOT_RESULTS.md
talk_slides.html

# Revise-and-resubmit correspondence, matched by shape rather than by exact
# name. A review cycle generates rebuttals, revised title pages and reviewer
# responses under names nobody can enumerate in advance, and every one of them
# carries the author's identity into a double-blind submission.
#
# `*[Mm]anuscript*` is deliberately broad: a revised draft under a directory
# nobody thought to exclude (paper2/, revision/, jqc_r1/) is the likeliest way
# the paper gets tracked again. No tracked file matches it today. If a genuine
# replication file ever needs one of these names, `git add -f` overrides.
*[Mm]anuscript*
*[Tt]itle_[Pp]age*
*[Cc]over_[Ll]etter*
*[Rr]ebuttal*
*[Rr]esponse*[Rr]eview*
*[Rr]esponse_to_*
*[Rr]eviewer*[Rr]esponse*

# --- manuscript generators ------------------------------------------------------
# These render the paper, its title page, the cover letter and the supplement
# from the master in paper/. None of them reproduces a number, none is called by
# regen_all.py, and all of them read inputs under paper/ or packages/ that are
# excluded above -- so in a fresh clone they could only fail on a missing file.
# They also embedded the author's name, city, email and ORCID directly in
# tracked source, which is how the title page stayed public after the file
# itself was untracked. make_plos_figs.py is deliberately NOT here: regen_all.py
# calls it and it only touches outputs/.
src/make_jqc_tex.py
src/make_general_tex.py
src/make_cover_letter.py
src/make_si.py
src/make_guide.py
